Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part III, first section. The Landau form of the effective potentials: what it \
is, how accurate it is, and why that matters\
\>", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"5eedc9b5-f64a-4f7e-b5ed-2e07778cd66e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part III of the solution builds the effective Lagrangians ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["CJT",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "cb4d3b97-c8c8-4ca2-a54f-378585b907e3"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["HS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f7bba5be-489a-484c-8ca0-a196a35d60f5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["KS",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "952ee34c-5848-477d-a945-d7eaf8544d6a"],
 " of the field of the superfluid boson singlet state. Their potential parts \
were summarized by a polynomial, the Landau form, with the remark: \"The \
Landau form is a fit; its largest residual is 0.27-0.7 % of the depth\". The \
author asked (21 November 2026) to explain this remark clearly and completely \
and why it is important, to define the Landau form with examples, and to keep \
the answer in the documents and in this notebook. This chapter is that \
answer. It is the first section of Part III in the notebook; the next chapter \
(Section III.T) is the second, and the other sections of Part III follow in \
the next versions. The computed curves are taken from the Rust program ",
 StyleBox["sf_part3",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " (the closed cell of Section III.L.3, with the SHA-256 checksums of its \
data files), and this chapter recomputes from them, by its own least squares, \
every number of the answer; the engine of Part II, which computes such \
states, is used by the next chapter."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fc23789-a662-4a97-a431-d1fa6bdff3b2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.1 The objects", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"81f40efd-e678-4468-b09e-0c73452f38a9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The field and its effective potential.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The field of the superfluid boson singlet state is the complex isospin \
vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "1"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "2"}]], ",", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "3"}]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e4b04111-173b-4832-b0b4-82a98af923d1"],
 " of the amplitudes of the pair self-energy of a uniform state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P",
      FontFamily->"Helvetica",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "\[Iota]",
     LimitsPositioning->True], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", "\[Iota]"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "819e5a62-b0e0-4c72-b937-a2da56438323"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["K",
     FontFamily->"Helvetica",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["LL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Iota]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca191c58-f746-4375-a724-72eac2f33081"],
 " are the three pair matrices of Part I (",
 StyleBox["kLL[iota]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro"],
 " in the code) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73fb9f8a-5e1e-48df-9b23-0799df89bb13"],
 " is one of the five computed methods: HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "53be849e-3595-48c7-a4a2-430937807717"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a13e98e-d7c7-47c6-9f8c-bf708fa32c7e"],
 ", HS ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "620b0c61-5105-4361-a5f1-6e24ed21878a"],
 " (the method of Hubbard and Stratonovich with the shares ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ddb90fc-01a1-4087-b74f-4ae4457ef848"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["HS",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
     StyleBox["V",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c87814-aa2d-4106-ad36-897090db7afd"],
 " of the scalar and the vector term decoupled in the density channels), KS \
(Kohn and Sham) and CJT (Cornwall, Jackiw and Tomboulis). The effective \
potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], ")"}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e91b0bdb-6fd8-4abe-a85f-3b9339e6a61b"],
 " is the smallest energy per volume of method ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2ab84f6-fbb4-44bd-b30b-a51b7df4d1ad"],
 " among the uniform states whose field is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03ae7131-85f1-46d2-9f0e-21a78d6dde80"],
 ", measured from the normal vacuum, so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", "0", ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fe06e063-038f-4482-9aba-7b6b44781ce9"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"616567bc-e38e-476e-9fa8-d4152d030cbe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How it is computed.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A fixed pair self-energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["a",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["K",
        FontFamily->"Helvetica",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["LL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "3"], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3bcb5f4-d705-4e25-a6dd-12100f10d1a8"],
 ", the applied field of amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c741ce6d-8d33-4bdf-9132-efb8ea8b6f2e"],
 ", is put into the matrix of Bogoliubov and de Gennes, the normal \
self-energy is made self-consistent, and the ground state gives one point: \
its own field ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c9c38b9-8c34-48a0-833a-496bc35e856c"],
 " and its energy per volume. The Rust program computes 61 points per method, \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["a",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bb35a04-0369-4166-9e36-24cacfa64f56"],
 " from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["0", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0909ba40-80d3-42fb-b319-e4c0b5ec9ec0"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a66eef1-1006-4a43-b354-89b2ffe391f0"],
 ", each self-consistent to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "13"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "584a1c57-cd03-432e-8817-813e833744d8"],
 ". Along the ",
 StyleBox["polar",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " fields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[CurlyTheta]"}]], "\[CapitalPhi]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8420b11a-9aa7-437e-9634-bb78609c7f0a"],
 " (real phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyTheta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "068ac2e6-3eae-4c4f-a826-0c43eed62387"],
 ", real unit vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31219c80-a651-4c42-9801-dd3585cb3ef2"],
 ") the potential depends on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalPhi]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f7bad5d3-fd37-48bb-8016-65d48bfad80f"],
 " alone. Its minimum lies at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", 
     StyleBox["SF",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7edb37b-3181-4ee7-ada4-6af6481b6375"],
 " (the vacuum), and the ",
 StyleBox["depth",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["SF",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], 
      StyleBox["X", "TI"]], 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", 
        StyleBox["SF",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
       StyleBox["X", "TI"]], ")"}]}], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d086ff19-e322-4d92-bf74-43555306c1ef"],
 " is the energy per volume by which the superfluid lies below the normal \
vacuum. The second derivative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["amp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "caf3c185-7bfb-41b1-863b-e62140ccccba"],
 " of the polar curve at its minimum fixes the mass of the amplitude mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SubsuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["SF",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["X", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["H",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], ")"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["amp",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[Prime]\[Prime]"], "/", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "+", 
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["SF",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["X", "TI"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5ed71b3-c78e-4155-8f86-240ad23baf19"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c3d93114-d0fa-40b2-85a1-22b971dbdbb3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["SF",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["X", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "943d72f0-bf43-4080-bd2a-d5652516cb99"],
 " are the two coefficients of the kinetic part of the effective Lagrangian."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5535efd2-6d04-4470-aaab-fda3d9eab0e9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["III.L.2 The Landau form: definition and examples", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4f225c04-52aa-4634-afdb-0f6bb7702df7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Definition.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A Landau form of a potential is its expansion in powers of the order \
parameter (the field that vanishes in the symmetric state and not in the \
broken one) under two rules: only polynomial invariants of the symmetry group \
occur, and the expansion stops after the lowest orders that bound the \
potential from below and produce its minima. L. D. Landau introduced it for \
phase transitions (1937): near a continuous transition the order parameter is \
small, the free energy is assumed to be analytic in it, and the form is its \
Taylor expansion, whose coefficients (the Landau coefficients) are \
derivatives at the symmetric state. The quadratic coefficient changes its \
sign at the transition; the signs of the higher coefficients decide the order \
of the transition and which broken state is the minimum. Examples:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49cf7cea-b7ba-48d7-8fe9-0413862d5df5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A uniaxial ferromagnet: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83a60fee-3430-450c-a71a-f4e3e42fcf54"],
 " for the magnetization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b37de35-b40d-40c3-86fe-4f9bf88f328b"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightArrow]", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["mag",
       FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6bcf76c-71a2-4a66-9c61-138fcdf8962a"],
 "), with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["mag",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5052d278-dee2-441c-a090-14be900493db"],
 " proportional to the temperature minus the Curie temperature and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6373b366-4bdf-43e3-a999-7616cfb087b1"],
 "; below the Curie temperature the minima are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["mag",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["mag",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", 
          SubscriptBox[
           StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["mag",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ff22f2d2-5b1b-484b-95f5-d5a6caf4e284"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"19c6931b-3b08-4231-9dc9-be69d46d060c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The theory of superconductivity of V. L. Ginzburg and L. D. Landau (1950): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
       StyleBox["GL",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b8bec446-d2f8-4e24-ab0e-fdd291417458"],
 " for the complex pair wave function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
    StyleBox["GL",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a22b1c3e-33fb-49a2-a933-1b643ffcec74"],
 " (the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "291721af-f9b5-412b-8680-ff72ce0fe1a6"],
 "), with gradient terms and the magnetic field added. L. P. Gor'kov (1959) \
derived it from the theory of Bardeen, Cooper and Schrieffer near the \
critical temperature, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", 
     StyleBox["GL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0e5260d0-c033-472a-9ce4-70280fa66657"],
 " is small; there the coefficients are true Taylor coefficients."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9d8caa4b-301c-4c2c-8970-6ade936755ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Higgs potential of the Standard Model, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Mu]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "2"]}], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
          StyleBox["SM",
           FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
       SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
        StyleBox["SM",
         FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], ")"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a299c95c-d74c-4034-8298-54ebd4d9c2fd"],
 ": the doublet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
    StyleBox["SM",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f1a3e44-cca1-4d42-8d9b-367a0ef5caf8"],
 " has the single invariant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
       StyleBox["SM",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]], ")"}], "\[Dagger]"], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", 
     StyleBox["SM",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d5b271ac-21c8-43e0-b724-fa7ad65653fc"],
 " of degree 2, and this Landau form is exact at tree level, not a truncation."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6ee0edf0-37c2-4c4e-8db1-69a18152520e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Bose-Einstein condensates of spin 1 (T.-L. Ho, 1998; T. Ohmi and K. \
Machida, 1998), the closest analogue of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43d14bad-c738-4e44-b49a-4f49b371c1df"],
 ": their order parameter is a complex vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9b5d64-7084-4a43-bff0-88115c7a7db8"],
 ", and their energy per volume ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "+", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
        "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d9db7f0-e51c-4f54-8d08-d13c8188d8e6"],
 " contains the same two quartic invariants as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d39321ec-1f48-459a-9b37-e835c7fed9f0"],
 ", the second term being the square of the spin. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a6c11891-ed71-4d64-b0b7-d6507fe8635c"],
 " (sodium-23) favors the polar state, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78a8231f-9df2-4aaf-8f52-602ef227135f"],
 " (rubidium-87) the ferromagnetic state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox["\[CurlyPi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Proportional]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", "0"}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0923aed6-74db-45ef-b29d-ff8a1352975d"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6bfe03cf-a361-464e-96b4-1d9bfcf4592f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ferroelectric barium titanate (A. F. Devonshire, 1949): ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "6"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d95b88d-b462-499c-bb8c-a2b0ee274d4d"],
 " for the polarization ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["D",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71d06839-cc15-4508-91e8-928493111361"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "<", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03cfd5d8-52ff-4bda-a049-04214bfbbde4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
     StyleBox["D",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], ">", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d1d006f-0c54-4634-9852-f496833d6e2d"],
 ": the sixth power is required, and the transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d90e19d8-dfd0-41bb-9090-cfd194de6ede"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Superfluid helium-3 (A. J. Leggett, 1975): one quadratic and five quartic \
invariants of a complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fa569aa-452a-4e75-81c7-277606b8b12b"],
 " matrix, whose five coefficients decide between the phases A and B. The \
nematic liquid crystals (P. G. de Gennes, 1971): the traceless symmetric \
tensor of the nematic order admits an invariant of the third degree, so the \
transition is of first order."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"398a137e-df2b-4a0e-ba14-0f79d1ccf0c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The name has nothing to do with the Landau levels of a charge in a magnetic \
field (Section I.6 of this notebook, AS2): the same physicist, another \
subject. ",
 StyleBox["The Landau form of $\\vec\\Phi$.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The symmetry is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["SU", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "2", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["v",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[Times]", 
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}], 
     StyleBox["LL",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["F",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26044d72-a48f-4512-a8ac-e5f82ba10c57"],
 ". The independent invariants up to the fourth degree are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c601e067-3e94-4288-bfbc-8925b2e7be85"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "fac385c9-4e70-4221-9788-5b7cef01fb09"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
     "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0201ad2a-6bf4-475a-9aa0-481af5670d6f"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "4"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "\[Times]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "\[RightVector]"], "*"]}], 
      "\[RightBracketingBar]"}], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSize->1.1 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "152af54a-d12e-4d18-8ad8-3162a5367c1a"],
 " vanishes exactly on the polar fields. The Landau form used by the solution \
is"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b2a09c7e-0430-4059-bdce-78ec8dc74d14"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
